From 5690d817ade8f7432fdc572be63ef3fdd07b501d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m03dev <m03dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:40:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add a test seam and offline coverage for systemOne's answer
 shaping

systemOne's answer shaping - the temperature buckets, softmax, per-question-type
output, rounding and usage accounting - was only exercised by the end-to-end test,
which runs only when the 1.7 GB ONNX bundle is on disk. sequence.ts is covered
without weights; this closes the other half.

- Laya.fromParts() builds an instance from already-open parts (session, tokenizer,
  config, ids), so the shaping can be driven by a stub session. It is a static
  factory calling the private constructor, so the public surface is unchanged and
  ordinary callers still use Laya.load().
- test/test_systemone.ts answers with a known logit pattern located through
  marker_mask, so a batched call with different option counts lines up, and checks
  each answer type, 4-decimal rounding, a tie's zero confidence, and that a
  single-question call matches the same question inside a batch.
- package.json adds the new test file to `yarn test`.

Run: yarn test (13 pass, 1 skipped), yarn typecheck, yarn lint - all clean.
